DOCK_AUDIT_RECORD=Audit record
HEADING_AUDIT_RECORD=Audit record
AUDIT_ADMIN_ONLY=Only administrators can read the audit record.
AUDIT_INTRO=What the server wrote down about the changes that matter: reservations, forced releases, arming of the jog, changes of the safety limits and global stops. Each line is chained to the one before it by a SHA-256, so a line changed or removed later shows when the chain is verified.
AUDIT_FILTER_LIMIT=Number of lines
AUDIT_ALL_TYPES=All types
AUDIT_ALL_ROBOTS=All robots
AUDIT_REFRESH=Refresh
AUDIT_VERIFY=Verify the chain
AUDIT_EXPORT=Export (.jsonl)
AUDIT_COL_SEQ=No.
AUDIT_COL_TIME=Time
AUDIT_COL_TYPE=Type
AUDIT_COL_OUTCOME=Outcome
AUDIT_COL_ACCOUNT=Account
AUDIT_COL_CONTROLLER=Window or device
AUDIT_COL_ADDRESS=Address
AUDIT_COL_ROBOT=Robot
AUDIT_COL_DETAIL=Detail
AUDIT_OUTCOME_OK=done
AUDIT_OUTCOME_REFUSED=refused
AUDIT_OUTCOME_FAILED=failed
AUDIT_TYPE_CLAIM=Reservation
AUDIT_TYPE_FORCE_CLAIM=Reservation taken over
AUDIT_TYPE_RELEASE=Release
AUDIT_TYPE_FORCE_RELEASE=Release forced
AUDIT_TYPE_JOG_ARM=Jog arming
AUDIT_TYPE_SAFETY_LIMITS=Safety limits
AUDIT_TYPE_STOP_ALL=Global STOP
AUDIT_FAILURE_NETWORK=The server could not be reached.
AUDIT_FAILURE_FORBIDDEN=This account is not an administrator: the server does not give it the audit record.
AUDIT_FAILURE_SESSION=Your session ended. Sign in again.
AUDIT_FAILURE_UNAVAILABLE=This server has no audit record (an older version, or it is not available).
AUDIT_FAILURE_OTHER=The server did not give the audit record.
AUDIT_LOCKED_OFF=The audit record is locked off by the environment of the server: nothing new is written.
AUDIT_SWITCHED_OFF=The audit record is switched off in the safety limits: nothing new is written.
AUDIT_EMPTY=No lines for this filter.
AUDIT_SERVER_OK=Server: the whole chain is intact ({count} lines).
AUDIT_SERVER_BROKEN=Server: the chain is BROKEN at line {seq} ({reason}).
AUDIT_LOCAL_OK=This program: {count} lines read, every hash matches, {links} links between neighbours checked, {gaps} gaps not comparable.
AUDIT_LOCAL_BROKEN_CHANGED=This program: line {seq} does not match its own hash - it was changed.
AUDIT_LOCAL_BROKEN_LINK=This program: line {seq} does not name the line before it - a line is missing or was replaced.
AUDIT_EXPORTED=Saved to {path}
AUDIT_EXPORT_FAILED=The file could not be written: {error}
ACCESS_CONDITIONAL_LABEL=Check that the robot has not changed
ACCESS_CONDITIONAL_STANDARD=Standard: reservations, table and one-off commands
ACCESS_CONDITIONAL_STRICT=Strict: every command except STOP
ACCESS_CONDITIONAL_OFF=Off: send commands without checking
ACCESS_CONDITIONAL_HINT=Each write carries the revision of the robot this program last saw; if someone else changed the robot in between, the server refuses it (412) and the robot is read again. Jog and speed are not checked in Standard because they repeat many times a second. STOP is never checked.
MSG_NET_REJ_REVISION={what} not applied: the robot changed since this program last read it (another operator or window). It was read again from the server: check it and repeat the action if it is still wanted.
MSG_ACCESS_REVISION_CHANGED={what} not applied: the robot changed since this program last read it (another operator or window). It was read again from the server: check it and try again. {detail}

# User accounts panel (administrators only)
DOCK_USERS=Users
HEADING_USERS=User accounts
USERS_ADMIN_ONLY=Only administrators can manage the accounts of the server.
USERS_INTRO=The accounts that can sign in to this server. An administrator can change settings, manage accounts and command robots; an operator can only command robots. Changing a name, a password or a role closes every session already open for that account.
USERS_COL_USERNAME=Username
USERS_COL_ROLE=Role
USERS_COL_CREATED=Created
USERS_REFRESH=Refresh
USERS_YOU=you
USERS_DELETE=Delete
