# Access options of the Server Admin screen (STUDIO parity)
HEADING_ADMIN_SECURITY=Access options
LBL_SECURITY_AI=Local AI relay (/api/ai/*)
SECURITY_AI_OPEN=Any signed-in user
SECURITY_AI_ADMIN=Administrators only
LBL_SECURITY_INFO=Ask for sign-in on the host information (metrics, process supervisor, ecosystem status)
MSG_SECURITY_INFO_OFF_CONFIRM=Turn the sign-in requirement off? The host information (metrics, process supervisor, ecosystem status) will be readable by anyone on the network.
SECURITY_INFO_OFF_WARNING=The host information is now readable by the whole network.
LBL_SECURITY_TLS=TLS (HTTPS / WSS)
PH_SECURITY_TLS_CERT=Path of the certificate file (PEM)
PH_SECURITY_TLS_KEY=Path of the key file (PEM)
SECURITY_TLS_PATHS_REQUIRED=To turn TLS on, give the path of the certificate and of the key.
LBL_SECURITY_TLS_FINGERPRINT=Certificate fingerprint (SHA-256)
SECURITY_TLS_ACTIVE=The running server uses TLS.
SECURITY_TLS_INACTIVE=The running server does not use TLS.
SECURITY_RESTART_NOTE=The change applies on the next restart.
SECURITY_SOURCE_ENV=Set in the environment of the server (locked)
SECURITY_SOURCE_CONFIG=Saved from this screen
SECURITY_SOURCE_DEFAULT=Default
SECURITY_SAVED=Saved.
LBL_SECURITY_BLE=Bluetooth LE (phones near the server)
SECURITY_BLE_OFF=Off
SECURITY_BLE_STATE=Phones read the state
SECURITY_BLE_COMMANDS=Phones read the state and send commands
LBL_SECURITY_BLE_ENCRYPTION=Ask for an encrypted Bluetooth link
SECURITY_BLE_RUNNING=The running server: {mode}.
MSG_SECURITY_BLE_UNENCRYPTED_CONFIRM=Allow commands over Bluetooth without an encrypted link? The access token of the account travels in every command, so anyone near the server could read it.
SECURITY_BLE_UNENCRYPTED_WARNING=Commands over Bluetooth are allowed without an encrypted link: anyone near the server could read the access tokens.
TITLE_SECURITY_INFO_OFF=Turn the sign-in requirement off
TITLE_SECURITY_BLE_UNENCRYPTED=Commands without an encrypted link
MSG_NET_OPERATOR_LOCAL_ONLY=This account is an operator: it can drive the robots, but the server accepts changes to the settings, the recorded points and the layout only from an administrator. What you changed stays in this window and is not saved.

